{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented in worktree impl-a01d-fanout. Extracted _fetch_project(client, queries) (symmetric to _enrich_project): drains both base queries for one project into a LOCAL list, merged into the shared snapshot ONLY on success (atomic — no partial/empty read leaks as deletions). Per-project try/except in _build_snapshot: transport error -> emit fetcher-project-fetch-failed alert (project + pass_id) + CONTINUE; SilentTruncationError/BackendPaginationStallError re-raise (fail loud); invalid key still fails closed in jql_active (626d). Single-project path (len==1: one key / unseeded fallback) fails CLOSED unchanged so it never writes an empty all-deletions snapshot (AC #3 regression parity; existing single-project + truncation-gate tests still pass). Added always-on unit test_one_project_base_query_failure_does_not_abort_pass (BAD raises HTTPError, OK returns issues): RED before fix, GREEN after; mutation check (revert isolation -> re-raise) returns RED. make lint + make typecheck clean; fetcher.py trimmed to 650 lines (module-size AC). One unrelated pre-existing env failure state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote (git cat-file exit 128 on temp bare repo) — reproduces on pristine origin/main."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786814205598047001,"uuid":"2c84f7c2-0b7c-4c17-85b2-1e4e44e2ec79"}